    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Question\n\nI added mini.pick to the [file selectors for avante.nvim](https://github.com/yetone/avante.nvim/blob/5ac934f2283d20ff805467d79ca6b4727eb0101e/lua/avante/file_selector.lua#L231-L238). However, it seems it was broken in [this PR](https://github.com/yetone/avante.nvim/pull/1153). I have fixed that by updating the code to:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nfunction FileSelector:mini_pick_ui(handler)\r\n  local success, mini_pick = pcall(require, \"mini.pick\")\r\n  if not success then\r\n    Utils.error(\"mini.pick is not installed. Please install mini.pick to use it as a file selector.\")\r\n    return\r\n  end\r\n  local result = mini_pick.builtin.files()\r\n  vim.notify(vim.inspect(result)) -- Just for verification.\r\n  if not result then\r\n    handler(nil)\r\n    return\r\n  end\r\n  handler(type(result) == \"string\" and { result } or result)\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis works, and I believe it would work with multi select, but when I select multiple with `<c-x>` then use `<m-cr>`, the function only returns current, but the selections are opened in quickfix.\r\n\r\nHow can I actually return selected files?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.pick</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I added mini.pick to the <a href=\"https://github.com/yetone/avante.nvim/blob/5ac934f2283d20ff805467d79ca6b4727eb0101e/lua/avante/file_selector.lua#L231-L238\">file selectors for avante.nvim</a>. However, it seems it was broken in <a href=\"https://github.com/yetone/avante.nvim/pull/1153\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/avante-corp/avante.nvim/pull/1153/hovercard\">this PR</a>. I have fixed that by updating the code to:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"function FileSelector:mini_pick_ui(handler)\n  local success, mini_pick = pcall(require, &quot;mini.pick&quot;)\n  if not success then\n    Utils.error(&quot;mini.pick is not installed. Please install mini.pick to use it as a file selector.&quot;)\n    return\n  end\n  local result = mini_pick.builtin.files()\n  vim.notify(vim.inspect(result)) -- Just for verification.\n  if not result then\n    handler(nil)\n    return\n  end\n  handler(type(result) == &quot;string&quot; and { result } or result)\nend\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">function</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">FileSelector</span>:<span class=\"pl-en\">mini_pick_ui</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">handler</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">success</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">mini_pick</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">pcall</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.pick<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">not</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">success</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">then</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">Utils</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">error</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.pick is not installed. Please install mini.pick to use it as a file selector.<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">result</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">mini_pick</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">builtin</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">files</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">notify</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">inspect</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">result</span>)) <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Just for verification.</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">not</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">result</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">then</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-c1\">handler</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">nil</span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">handler</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">type</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">result</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>string<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">and</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">result</span> } <span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">result</span>)\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This works, and I believe it would work with multi select, but when I select multiple with <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;c-x&gt;</code> then use <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;m-cr&gt;</code>, the function only returns current, but the selections are opened in quickfix.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">How can I actually return selected files?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.pick\nQuestion\nI added mini.pick to the file selectors for avante.nvim. However, it seems it was broken in this PR. I have fixed that by updating the code to:\nfunction FileSelector:mini_pick_ui(handler)\n  local success, mini_pick = pcall(require, \"mini.pick\")\n  if not success then\n    Utils.error(\"mini.pick is not installed. Please install mini.pick to use it as a file selector.\")\n    return\n  end\n  local result = mini_pick.builtin.files()\n  vim.notify(vim.inspect(result)) -- Just for verification.\n  if not result then\n    handler(nil)\n    return\n  end\n  handler(type(result) == \"string\" and { result } or result)\nend\nThis works, and I believe it would work with multi select, but when I select multiple with <c-x> then use <m-cr>, the function only returns current, but the selections are opened in quickfix.\nHow can I actually return selected files?",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
