            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The returned value of `MiniPick.start()` is indeed [the item that was current when is stopped](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/509e086e13a1aa7105e427bb1b122a7174716b77/doc/mini-pick.txt#L851). For the common case of choosing an item with \"choose\" action (`<CR>` by default) it is indeed the chosen item, hence the design.\r\n\r\nA more idiomatic approach to this would be to define custom [`source.choose`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/509e086e13a1aa7105e427bb1b122a7174716b77/doc/mini-pick.txt#L406) and [`source.choose_marked`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/509e086e13a1aa7105e427bb1b122a7174716b77/doc/mini-pick.txt#L435) and supply it to `MiniPick.builtin.files` directly. So something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nfunction FileSelector:mini_pick_ui(handler)\r\n  if not _G.MiniPick then\r\n    Utils.error('mini.pick is not set up. Please install and set up mini.pick to use it as a file selector.')\r\n    return\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  local choose = function(item) handler(type(item) == 'string' and { item } or item) end\r\n  local choose_marked = function(items_marked) handler(items_marked) end\r\n  local source = { choose = choose, choose_marked = choose_marked }\r\n  local result = MiniPick.builtin.files(nil, { source = source })\r\n  if result == nil then handler(nil) end\r\nend\r\n```",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">The returned value of <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniPick.start()</code> is indeed <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/509e086e13a1aa7105e427bb1b122a7174716b77/doc/mini-pick.txt#L851\">the item that was current when is stopped</a>. For the common case of choosing an item with \"choose\" action (<code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;CR&gt;</code> by default) it is indeed the chosen item, hence the design.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">A more idiomatic approach to this would be to define custom <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/509e086e13a1aa7105e427bb1b122a7174716b77/doc/mini-pick.txt#L406\"><code class=\"notranslate\">source.choose</code></a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/509e086e13a1aa7105e427bb1b122a7174716b77/doc/mini-pick.txt#L435\"><code class=\"notranslate\">source.choose_marked</code></a> and supply it to <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniPick.builtin.files</code> directly. So something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"function FileSelector:mini_pick_ui(handler)\n  if not _G.MiniPick then\n    Utils.error('mini.pick is not set up. Please install and set up mini.pick to use it as a file selector.')\n    return\n  end\n\n  local choose = function(item) handler(type(item) == 'string' and { item } or item) end\n  local choose_marked = function(items_marked) handler(items_marked) end\n  local source = { choose = choose, choose_marked = choose_marked }\n  local result = MiniPick.builtin.files(nil, { source = source })\n  if result == nil then handler(nil) end\nend\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">function</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">FileSelector</span>:<span class=\"pl-en\">mini_pick_ui</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">handler</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">not</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">_G</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">MiniPick</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">then</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">Utils</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">error</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.pick is not set up. Please install and set up mini.pick to use it as a file selector.<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">choose</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">item</span>) <span class=\"pl-c1\">handler</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">type</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">item</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>string<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">and</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">item</span> } <span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">item</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">choose_marked</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">items_marked</span>) <span class=\"pl-c1\">handler</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">items_marked</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">source</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">choose</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">choose</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">choose_marked</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">choose_marked</span> }\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">result</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">builtin</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">files</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">nil</span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">source</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">source</span> })\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">result</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">nil</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">then</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">handler</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">nil</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span></pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "The returned value of MiniPick.start() is indeed the item that was current when is stopped. For the common case of choosing an item with \"choose\" action (<CR> by default) it is indeed the chosen item, hence the design.\nA more idiomatic approach to this would be to define custom source.choose and source.choose_marked and supply it to MiniPick.builtin.files directly. So something like this:\nfunction FileSelector:mini_pick_ui(handler)\n  if not _G.MiniPick then\n    Utils.error('mini.pick is not set up. Please install and set up mini.pick to use it as a file selector.')\n    return\n  end\n\n  local choose = function(item) handler(type(item) == 'string' and { item } or item) end\n  local choose_marked = function(items_marked) handler(items_marked) end\n  local source = { choose = choose, choose_marked = choose_marked }\n  local result = MiniPick.builtin.files(nil, { source = source })\n  if result == nil then handler(nil) end\nend",
